{
    "background_story": "Mathew was a seasoned fisherman who had spent his entire life on the waters of the North Sea. He knew every hidden cove and every school of fish that swam beneath the surface. But despite his years of experience, Mathew had a peculiar affinity for flounder. He loved the way they lay flat on the ocean floor, their camouflage a testament to their adaptability. Mathew's fishing boat, the 'Flounder's Fancy', was a familiar sight in the harbor, and locals would often joke that he had a sixth sense for finding the elusive flatfish. One day, while out on a solo trip, Mathew hauled in a massive flounder, the biggest anyone in the village had ever seen. From that day on, he was known as the 'Flounder King', and his reputation as a master fisherman was cemented.",
